# QUESTION: Does a real ze hub record live fleet events (device.connect,
# config.fetch, config.ack, config.push, device.disconnect), ingest and
# deduplicate device offline mode-change receipts over fleet-audit-receipts,
# serve show fleet audit with device/type/since pipes over SSH CLI, and preserve
# monotonic audit sequence order across a hub restart?
# WHY NOT A UNIT TEST: end-to-end TLS authentication, hub write-observer
# config-changed delivery, async ZeFS page and manifest persistence on disk,
# SSH CLI pipe dispatch, and post-restart recovery with monotonic sequence
# continuation run through the real ze hub daemon and its disk ZeFS store.
# VALIDATES: spec-fleet-3 AC-1, AC-2, AC-3, AC-4, AC-6, AC-7, AC-8, AC-9,
# AC-10, AC-12, AC-14. The fixture connects edge-01 to a real hub, verifies
# newest-first entries and device/type/since pipes over SSH CLI, triggers a
# config push, sends and replays a fleet-audit-receipts batch to prove
# deduplication with actor device:edge-01, disconnects edge-01, restarts the
# hub on the same disk store, and verifies exact preservation plus monotonic
# sequence continuation on reconnect.
option=storage:value=disk
option=timeout:value=180s
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture managed/fleet-audit-log $PORT $PORT2 $PORT3:timeout=180s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: fleet audit log recorded live events, filtered by device/type/since, deduplicated receipts, and survived hub restart
